<!--
  The Quota: the campaign start. The fifth scenario, and the only one with a story.

  The other four starts are sandboxes and stay that way (the user's call,
  2026-11-14). This one switches on GameComponent_Campaign through ScenPart_Campaign
  (Source/RimRising/Campaign.cs), which then tells a story in acts: a quota, a
  reprisal, a stranger, a hunt, a rising, the Rain. Every act waits for its own
  condition, and the key beats are offers the player may refuse.

  WHAT IS DIFFERENT FROM "UP FROM THE MINE", and why:

  - TRUE SIGILS, not forged ones. The Lurcher hunt comes for a sigil that does not
    match its bearer. Breakout's Reds carry forged paper from the first day, so the
    hunters would already be coming before the story gave them a reason. Here the
    clan is exactly what its paper says, and the mismatch walks in later.
  - A WORKING RIG. The quota is helium-3, a deep resource. The director places a
    clawDrill over a seeded seam with a wood-fired generator beside it, and the two
    research projects below are what a clan that runs such a rig already knows.
    Without that the quota would be a letter about work nobody could do.
  - FOUR REDS, fed and supplied. A clan on its claim, not survivors of a flood.

  STRUCTURE mirrored from Scenarios_RimRising.xml in this folder (Breakout for the
  xenotype page, arrival method and starting things; Household for
  ScenPart_StartingResearch). ScenPartDef mirrored from RR_StartingSigils in
  Defs/Carving/Sigils.xml; category Rule is what vanilla's own CreateIncident part
  uses (Core/Defs/Scenarios/ScenParts_Various.xml). Electricity and DeepDrilling are
  vanilla research defNames, checked in Core/Defs/ResearchProjectDefs.

  All text is original. "The Laurel", "helldiver" and "clan" are setting terms, used
  the way the mod already uses them; no scene from the books is retold.
-->
<Defs>

  <ScenPartDef>
    <defName>RR_CampaignPart</defName>
    <label>the campaign</label>
    <scenPartClass>RimRising.ScenPart_Campaign</scenPartClass>
    <category>Rule</category>
    <selectionWeight>0</selectionWeight>
    <summaryPriority>459</summaryPriority>
  </ScenPartDef>

  <ScenarioDef ParentName="ScenarioBase">
    <defName>RR_Scenario_Quota</defName>
    <label>The Quota (campaign)</label>
    <description>Four Reds, a drill, and a number.

The clan has worked this claim for longer than anyone in it has been alive. The helium comes up, the Society's tithe-men take it away, and every quarter there is a notice: the clan that beats its quota wins the Laurel. Extra rations. Better quarters. Proof that the work is seen.

Your clan has never won it. This quarter, people have started saying it out loud - that this time the numbers are there, if everyone digs.

This start tells a story. It unfolds in acts as your colony lives through them, and the turning points arrive as offers you are free to refuse. Refuse the important one and the story ends quietly; the colony carries on as an ordinary one.</description>
    <scenario>
      <summary>A Red mining clan, a helium quota, and what comes of meeting it. A story told in acts.</summary>
      <parts>

        <li Class="ScenPart_GameStartDialog">
          <def>GameStartDialog</def>
          <text>The rig is already warm. It is always already warm.

Somewhere above you, people you will never meet have decided how much helium this ground owes them. The number will arrive in a day or two, the way it always does, and the clan will do what it has always done.

Dig. That part, at least, you know how to do.</text>
          <closeSound>GameStartSting</closeSound>
        </li>

        <li Class="ScenPart_ConfigPage_ConfigureStartingPawns_Xenotypes">
          <def>ConfigurePawnsXenotypes</def>
          <pawnChoiceCount>10</pawnChoiceCount>
          <customSummary>Start with four Reds.</customSummary>
          <xenotypeCounts>
            <li>
              <xenotype>RR_Red</xenotype>
              <count>4</count>
              <description>Red</description>
              <requiredAtStart>true</requiredAtStart>
              <allowedDevelopmentalStages>Adult</allowedDevelopmentalStages>
            </li>
          </xenotypeCounts>
        </li>

        <li Class="ScenPart_PlayerPawnsArriveMethod">
          <def>PlayerPawnsArriveMethod</def>
          <visible>false</visible>
          <method>Standing</method>
        </li>

        <!-- What a clan that runs a rig already knows. -->
        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingResearch">
          <def>StartingResearch</def>
          <project>Electricity</project>
        </li>
        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingResearch">
          <def>StartingResearch</def>
          <project>DeepDrilling</project>
        </li>

        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingThing_Defined">
          <def>StartingThing_Defined</def>
          <thingDef>RR_Weapon_SlingBlade</thingDef>
          <count>4</count>
        </li>
        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingThing_Defined">
          <def>StartingThing_Defined</def>
          <thingDef>MealSimple</thingDef>
          <count>30</count>
        </li>
        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingThing_Defined">
          <def>StartingThing_Defined</def>
          <thingDef>MedicineHerbal</thingDef>
          <count>10</count>
        </li>
        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingThing_Defined">
          <def>StartingThing_Defined</def>
          <thingDef>Steel</thingDef>
          <count>250</count>
        </li>
        <!-- The generator beside the rig burns wood; this is its first fortnight. -->
        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingThing_Defined">
          <def>StartingThing_Defined</def>
          <thingDef>WoodLog</thingDef>
          <count>400</count>
        </li>
        <li Class="ScenPart_StartingThing_Defined">
          <def>StartingThing_Defined</def>
          <thingDef>ComponentIndustrial</thingDef>
          <count>6</count>
        </li>

        <!-- True sigils: the clan is what its paper says (ScenPart_Sigils.cs). -->
        <li Class="RimRising.ScenPart_Sigils">
          <def>RR_StartingSigils</def>
        </li>

        <!-- The story itself (Campaign.cs). -->
        <!-- quota: canisters of helium-3 owed; quotaDays: days to mine them. Measured
             in rrtestmode=campaignstart, one Red on the rig brings up about 90 a day,
             so 900 in twelve days wants someone drilling most of the time. -->
        <li Class="RimRising.ScenPart_Campaign">
          <def>RR_CampaignPart</def>
          <quota>900</quota>
          <quotaDays>12</quotaDays>
        </li>

      </parts>
    </scenario>
  </ScenarioDef>

</Defs>
